						 <div style="text-align: center;"></div> <div style="float:right; margin:0 2em 1em 2em; width:300px; border:0;"> <table class="wiki-content-table"> <tr> <td colspan="2"><img src="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6a/Common_daisy.JPG" width="300px" alt="Common_daisy.JPG" class="image" /></td> </tr> <tr> <td colspan="2">SCP-XXXX specimens in ███████, Canada</td> </tr> </table> </div> <div class="anom-bar-container item-5968 clear-2 keter none keneq notice {$american}"> <div class="anom-bar"> <div class="top-box"> <div class="top-left-box"><span class="item">Item#:</span> <span class="number">5968</span></div> <div class="top-center-box"> <div class="bar-one"></div> <div class="bar-two"></div> <div class="bar-three"></div> <div class="bar-four"></div> <div class="bar-five"></div> <div class="bar-six"></div> </div> <div class="top-right-box"> <div class="level">Level2</div> <div class="clearance"></div> </div> </div> <div class="bottom-box"> <div class="text-part"> <div class="main-class"> <div class="contain-class"> <div class="class-category">Containment Class:</div> <div class="class-text">keter</div> </div> <div class="second-class"> <div class="class-category">Secondary Class:</div> <div class="class-text">none</div> </div> </div> <div class="disrupt-class"> <div class="class-category">Disruption Class:</div> <div class="class-text">keneq</div> </div> <div class="risk-class"> <div class="class-category">Risk Class:</div> <div class="class-text">notice</div> </div> </div> <div class="diamond-part"> <div class="danger-diamond"><a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/classification-committee-memo">link to memo</a><br /> <div class="arrows"></div> <div class="octagon"></div> <div class="quadrants"> <div class="top-quad"></div> <div class="right-quad"></div> <div class="left-quad"></div> <div class="bottom-quad"></div> </div> <div class="top-icon"></div> <div class="right-icon"></div> <div class="left-icon"></div> <div class="bottom-icon"></div> </div> </div> </div> </div> </div> <p><strong>Special Containment Procedures:</strong> In all the places where SCP-5986 specimens have been found, a wall is to be built around them, restricting access from the public. Places where SCP-XXXX can grow are to be monitored daily by MTF Theta-4 (“Gardeners”) for specimens.</p> <p><strong>Description:</strong> SCP-5986 is a species of plant, known to the public as <em>Artica flora</em>. Massive data about SCP-5986 is known to the public due to it having a similar appearance to <em>Bellis perris</em><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-476264-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" >1</a></sup> and it being found by Canadians. SCP-5986 can only grow in areas with a temperature of less than, or equal to, 4°C.</p> <p>SCP-5986 possesses multiple anomalous abilities:</p> <ul> <li>Able to produce seeds, seemingly forever, leading to mass population</li> <li>Able to drop the temperature around it down to up to -53°C</li> <li>Able to launch it’s seeds with distances up to 500 meters at rates of 102 mph</li> <li>Able to make the surrounding area pile up with up to 60&#160;cm of snow</li> <li>Able to survive on any solid object, as long as it’s surface temperature less than, or equal to, -90°C</li> <li>Sentience and sapience</li> </ul> <p>Using genetic testing, specimens of SCP-5986 seems to have been around for 500,000 years, if not longer.</p> <p><strong>Incident Log-5986:</strong> The following is text found in a journal in ███████, Canada. The journal was found in an excavation, unrelated to the foundation.</p> <blockquote> <p style="text-align: center;">9th Feb, 1840</p> <p>Today I found something strange out while hunting. I’m in Canada right? Cold, freezing. Daisies, they’re supposed to grow in warmer places, from what I’ve heard. I wouldn’t know too much would I? But, today I found a daisy! Right here in ███████, a daisy! Well, other than that, not seen nothing strange.</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p style="text-align: center;">10th Feb, 1840</p> <p>Found more of them daisies. At least 10. I tried to pick one of them, give it to my daughter but the others shot seeds at me like arrows. You believe it? What next, finding sunflowers on the Himilayas?</p> </blockquote> <blockquote> <p style="text-align: center;">11th Feb, 1840</p> <p>Today I came home with cuts and bruises. Any guesses? Those darn daisies! Kept hitting me ‘til I was forced to retreated. Still stings like mad though. I think I’ll stay well away from hunting now. Maybe kill those things.</p> </blockquote> <p>by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thekidnamedcover" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=7141604&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608647172" alt="TheKidNamedCover" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=7141604)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/thekidnamedcover" >TheKidNamedCover</a></span></p> <div class="footnotes-footer"> <div class="title">Footnotes</div> <div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-476264-1"><a href="javascript:;" >1</a>. Common daisy</div> </div> 
